    <record>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-156-stamp-freshness.md (inventory, live checks, rule, interpretations xii-xxii, placement justification, tests)</record>
    <summary>
      (1) Derivation: CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns makes a child's stamp the root of WHATEVER it is filed under (communication / event / to-do / analysis: the four sprk_regarding{core}; invoice and budget: typed matter / project; document: the shared DocumentLinkFields root links; agreement and report card: sprk_regarding matter / project). Two different roots of one type = error. ClassifyStampSource is the one pair-based rule the cascade, the job and the resolver share.
      (2) Cascade: CoreAncestorRestamper.AfterWriteAsync is called after the write by PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}, associate-record, UpdateRecordActionCore (playbook node + ActionSeam), DataverseUpdateHandler and the field-mapping push; it writes only the stamp columns of the root types the source can carry, never a direct link or the owner; transitive (depth 4; cycles converge); a child failure is reported, the caller's write stands. The user-OBO AI update tool ENQUEUES the cascade (interpretation xvii).
      (3) Job: CoreAncestorStampReconciliationJob, ADR-036 IScheduledJob every 5 minutes (AddScheduledJob, unconditional): repairs stale copies and F-051-6 orphans; failed scan = failed run; claim per repair, completion marker scoped to the run; report-only switch CoreAncestor:StampReconciliation:WritesEnabled=false.
      (4) Enqueue: CoreAncestorRestampQueue + CoreAncestorRestampJobHandler (ADR-004, sdap-jobs, lazy Service Bus).
      (5) Resolver: 155's held branch replaced by the live comparison — equal resolves like a direct root; differ = 409 container_ancestor_stale + enqueue (transient for the inbound processor); unreadable 503; missing 409; transitive; filing loop 409; a secure securable source is a root; two roots of one type on a source = ambiguous. Office carrier: agree = direct link; differ + any secure = ambiguous; differ + none secure = direct link. Still held: service request; intermediates on rows that carry no copy; a pair alone naming an intermediate.
    </summary>
    <escalations>Neither trigger fired. Trigger 1: no path needs a transaction Dataverse lacks — in the window between an intermediate's write and its children's PATCHes the resolver refuses a stale copy (409), it never misfiles. Trigger 2: live max 2 stamped children under any one intermediate (cascade bounded at 5000 per table, depth 4; past it TRUNCATED and the job finishes). FLAGGED for the owner (not an escalation): interpretation xvii — DataverseUpdateRecordHandler's own MUST rule forbids an app-only client, so its cascade is enqueued (seconds) rather than run in the same operation; and xii — the TypeScript stamp mirror still derives only the four columns (client-created children under invoice / document / agreement / budget / report card are unstamped until the job's next run).</escalations>
    <step-9-5>
      <code-review>Self-review over every changed file. Fixed: (a) job completion marker keyed by row + value suppressed a NEW staleness for 30 minutes (the manual live gate's second step would have failed) — now scoped to the run (xix); (b) after-write enqueues collapsed per minute — now one message per write (xx); (c) associate-record parsed the document id only after the write — now before; (d) two roots of one type on a source answered stale (a refresh that never comes) — now ambiguous, with a test (xxii); (e) NetArchTest DocumentLinkVocabularyGuardTests caught hard-coded document link columns — both resolvers now project Spaarke.Dataverse.DocumentLinkFields, and ChildAncestorLinks refuses to load a link to an unclassified type (xxi); (f) stale comments in OBOEndpoints and IncomingCommunicationProcessor updated. No open findings.</code-review>
      <adr-check>ADR-002 (no plugins; WP-1 one owner = CoreAncestorResolver + restamper; WP-5 fix-up job) compliant. ADR-003 fail closed: compliant (stale / ambiguous / unresolved refusals; failed scan = failed run; never a shared container while a secure root may be involved). ADR-004: handler idempotent (re-derives at write time), Failure then Poisoned. ADR-010: concrete singletons, no new interface. ADR-013: AI code calls Dataverse services, never the reverse. ADR-032: every registration unconditional. ADR-034: each derivation stays one hop. ADR-036 A1-1..A1-7: AddScheduledJob, claim + run-scoped marker, no throw (the next tick revisits everything), heartbeat per attempt, host-neutral, cancellation honoured. ADR-038: KEEP paths, no banned patterns. ADR-052: BFF (schedule = IScheduledJob, queue = IJobHandler). No violations; no section 6.5 path needed.</adr-check>
    </step-9-5>
    <placement>All new types in Sprk.Bff.Api Services/Dataverse beside the invariant's owner; no new package, endpoint, interface, option class or plugin; three-question justification table in the note. Publish size: code only — the fresh-worktree master-vs-branch measurement (CLAUDE.md section 10 item 4) is left to the main session, as in task 155. No package change, so no new CVE surface.</placement>
